2026-08-30T13:21Z claude note RECALL AND FUSION MEASURED, real data, doudou (CPU), all 18 surviving (candidate, rung) cells. Subsample: seeded whole-item shuffle (seed 20260830, `bench/build_recall_subsample.py`), 33 items / 1 533 of the 2 100 items / 93 022 passages in the real corpus — sized from 0263's own measured per-passage embedding cost (7 980,1 ms summed across the 18 surviving cells), which would put a 10k-passage campaign at ~22 h serial; even at 1 533 passages the run took 3 h 07 (12:12-15:19 CEST), CPU-shared with ticket 0266's concurrent campaign on the same machine. Keyword arm (FTS5/bm25, `bench/fts5_keyword_arm.mjs`, shared across every cell, never rebuilt per cell): recall@30 0,8092, MRR 0,9478, 400 probes, 0 zero-hit. Vector arm (`bench/recall_embed.mjs` + `bench/vec_task_recall.mjs`, passage-role template applied — unlike the 0263 fidelity vectors, which carry none): every candidate's fp32/q8/uint8 recall sits at 0,86-0,93 EXCEPT granite-97m-multilingual-r2 q8, which collapses to 0,5895 (from 0,9025 at fp32) — the real-world cost of 0263's already-worst-quantizing fidelity cell (q8 cos_mean 0,743121, overlap_at_30_mean 0,2349); its own uint8 rung loses far less (0,8644). Fused arm (RRF k=60, `bench/fused_recall.mjs`; frac=1 for both arms — DESIGN §2.6's own upper bound, plain RRF, since #6012-style frac_vec calibration is ticket 0031's and has no data source yet): every healthy cell's fused recall sits between keyword-alone and vector-alone. Across the 17 healthy cells, vector-arm gain over keyword-alone ranges 0,0552-0,1202 and fused gain ranges 0,0550-0,0812; on average about three-quarters of the isolated vector-arm gain survives fusion (mean fraction 0,7352, median 0,7236) — never the whole of it, confirming the tracker's expectation that a vector-arm win washes out against an unchanged keyword arm. granite-97m q8 disagrees more sharply than a smaller fraction: fused recall 0,7454 beats its own broken vector arm (0,5895) but still LOSES to keyword alone (fused_gain_over_keyword -0,0638) — at that rung, fusing the vector arm in makes retrieval WORSE than keyword search by itself. `bench/results/0070-cosine-fusion/` is loop fusion (an arithmetic optimisation of the cosine scan), unrelated to this RRF search-result fusion. fp32-against-itself control: 1,0 for every candidate, reused from 0263 (not re-measured here). Deviation from the ticket's illustrative subsample size: 1 533 passages, not 10-20k — justified above by a real measured cost, not assumed; comparability is within-campaign (identical subsample/probes/gap/topk/seed for every cell), not against `0025-x1-recall/`. `bench/build_0265_summary.py` cross-checks `fused_recall.mjs`'s own vector-arm reimplementation against `vec_task_recall.mjs`'s canonical output for all 18 cells: exact agreement, 0 mismatches. Committed: `bench/results/0265-recall-fusion/{model}__{dtype}.json` (18 cells), `SUMMARY.json`, `keyword-arm.json`; raw vectors/corpus stay out of git under `/home/haduong/data/projets/zoteus-bench/0265/`. `tests/test_recall_fusion_0265.py` adds the dtype-provenance guard the Test section asks for, plus the fp32 self-control check against 0263's own artifact, plus fast fixture tests of the shared probe-draw logic.

